# __PROJECT_NAME__

Build with the included Maven Wrapper and JDK 21; no global Maven is required. On PowerShell use `./mvnw.cmd` instead of `./mvnw` and quote `-D...` arguments. Framework artifacts are prepared by the repository Runner; rerun it without `--skipInstall` after changing the framework.
This local ranking season project was generated by zeroServer `scripts/NewLocalGame.java --template ranking-season`.

## Run

First install the current zeroServer SNAPSHOT into the local Maven repository:

~~~powershell
./mvnw -q -DskipTests install
~~~

Then run these commands in this project directory:

~~~powershell
./mvnw -q clean test
./mvnw -q exec:java
~~~

Expected output:

~~~text
ranking-season=ok|mode=local|name=__PROJECT_NAME__|summary=season=season-2,players=1,top=1001:300,player=1001,rank=1,score=300,resets=1,lastAction=rank:1001=1|logs=9|metrics=8|maxProtocolId=95107
~~~

